{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2014-9939",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: buffer overflow in ihex.c"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ihex.c in GNU Binutils before 2.26 contains a stack buffer overflow when printing bad bytes in Intel Hex objects."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2014-9939",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2014-9939\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: gdb\nFixed Version: 7.10-1\nLink: [CVE-2014-9939](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2014-9939)\nihex.c in GNU Binutils before 2.26 contains a stack buffer overflow when printing bad bytes in Intel Hex objects.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2014-9939**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|gdb|7.10-1|[CVE-2014-9939](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2014-9939)|\n\nihex.c in GNU Binutils before 2.26 contains a stack buffer overflow when printing bad bytes in Intel Hex objects."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2014-8501",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "binutils: out-of-bounds write when parsing specially crafted PE executable"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The _bfd_XXi_swap_aouthdr_in function in bfd/peXXigen.c in GNU binutils 2.24 and earlier allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (out-of-bounds write) and possibly have other unspecified impact via a crafted NumberOfRvaAndSizes field in the AOUT header in a PE executable."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2014-8501",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2014-8501\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: gdb\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2014-8501](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2014-8501)\nThe _bfd_XXi_swap_aouthdr_in function in bfd/peXXigen.c in GNU binutils 2.24 and earlier allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (out-of-bounds write) and possibly have other unspecified impact via a crafted NumberOfRvaAndSizes field in the AOUT header in a PE executable.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2014-8501**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|gdb||[CVE-2014-8501](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2014-8501)|\n\nThe _bfd_XXi_swap_aouthdr_in function in bfd/peXXigen.c in GNU binutils 2.24 and earlier allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (out-of-bounds write) and possibly have other unspecified impact via a crafted NumberOfRvaAndSizes field in the AOUT header in a PE executable."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.75.0"
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CVE-2014-9939",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Package: binutils\nInstalled Version: 0.0.1-1\nVulnerability CVE-2014-9939\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nFixed Version: 2.25.90.20151125-1\nLink: [CVE-2014-9939](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2014-9939)"
          },
